This module defines the concepts and the principal properties that will be reused in other modules. In particular, the module designs the aspects related to a service provider who manages the IoT devices in the urban area, the service usage by the users and the modelling of an IoT device which collects and sends data.

## Introduction back to ToC

The ontology suite for the Urban IoT Devices was developed to support the integration and the publication of different data from different service providers who manage the IoT devices in the urban area. The ontologies were developed for the Comune di Milano (Italy), but they are generic and can be applied to any city.

The Core module (http://www.w3id.org/urban-iot/core) defines classes and properties related to the service providers, to the IoT devices, to the service users, and to the data collected from the devices on their usage. The concepts defined from the Core module are expressed at high level and are declined in the specific domain inside the other modules in the suite that imports it (for example, Sharing Mobility module (http://www.w3id.org/urban-iot/sharing) and Electric Mobility module (http://www.w3id.org/urban-iot/electric).

Service users are modeled as uiot:ServiceUser and can be uiot:ServicePrivateUser, namely physical persons (subclass of schema:Person) subscribed to a service, or uiot:ServiceBusinessUser namely legal entity (subclass of legal:LegalEntity) subscribed to a business contract. Only a uiot:ServicePrivateUser can performs a uiot:UsageSession. A uiot:ServiceBusinessUser can enable a list of uiot:ServicePrivateUser to the service usage and to be associated to a usage session. However, it is not necessary to specify the physical person that used the service by the specific business contract.

Image: Core

The following two diagrams provide a detailed description of the previous one, specifying further properties that are defined or reused to describe the presented concepts.

A uiot:UsageSession is a schema:Event from which it inherits the description in terms of starting instant, ending instant and duration. A usage session can be also associated to a boolean value for the property uiot:reservationUsed that specifies if the session has been booked in advance by the user.

A uiot:ServiceUser is modeled by an anonymous identifier (dct:identifier), by the date of subscription to the service (uiot:registrationDate) and in case by the date of subscription cancellation from the service (uiot:deregistrationDate). A uiot:ServiceUser is associated to a schema:Service to which it is registered through the property uiot:registeredTo. It can be also associated to other services for which the same subscription enables the usage (e.g., working car sharing services in more cities) in the moment he makes at least one uiot:UsageSession for that service.

